1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
So welcome back.
欢迎回来。

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:16,040
It's a great honor to introduce a mathematical legend.
有幸介绍一位数学传奇人物。

3
00:00:16,040 --> 00:00:25,080
John Milnor, who as an undergraduate showed that the integral of the curvature of a knot
John Milnor，在本科期间证明了纽结曲率的积分

4
00:00:25,120 --> 00:00:34,120
was at least four pi, and became very famous as a result,
结果至少为四π，并因此而非常著名，

5
00:00:34,120 --> 00:00:42,120
won the Fields Medal at the age of 31, was professor at Princeton and the Institute for Advanced Study,
在31岁时获得了菲尔兹奖，曾在普林斯顿大学和高等研究院任教，

6
00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:48,120
and is now director of the Center for Mathematical Research at Stony Brook,
现在是石溪数学研究所的主任，

7
00:00:48,120 --> 00:00:54,120
and is a recipient of many honors, including the National Medal of Science,
并且获得过许多荣誉，包括国家科学奖章，

8
00:00:54,160 --> 00:00:58,160
We'll introduce the next speaker.
我们将介绍下一位演讲者。

9
00:00:58,160 --> 00:01:05,160
Jack Milnor, go ahead.
Jack Milnor，请发言。

10
00:01:05,160 --> 00:01:10,160
Well, it's a great pleasure to introduce Vladimir Voevodsky.
非常荣幸地向大家介绍 Vladimir Voevodsky。

11
00:01:10,160 --> 00:01:16,160
Voevodsky began his mathematical career in Moscow, and then came here to Harvard as a junior fellow,
开始他的数学生涯在莫斯科，然后作为初级研究员来到哈佛，

12
00:01:16,160 --> 00:01:23,160
and after a few years at Northwestern, is now at the Institute for Advanced Study.
在西北大学工作几年后，现在在高等研究院。

13
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:30,200
And as you all know, he was recently awarded a Fields Medal for his work on motivic homotopy theory.
而你们都知道，他最近因为对母题同伦论的工作获得了菲尔兹奖。

14
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:39,200
This is a marvelous development which introduces ideas and methods from homotopy theory into pure algebra,
这是一个美妙的发展，它将同伦理论的思想和方法引入纯粹代数，

15
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:45,200
and gives an essential new tool for solving algebraic problems.
为解决代数问题提供了必不可少的新工具。

16
00:01:45,200 --> 00:01:49,200
So it's a great pleasure to introduce Voevodsky.
所以很荣幸介绍 Voevodsky。

17
00:01:49,240 --> 00:02:02,240
Hello, thank you very much for, thank you, Jack, for the introduction.
你好，非常感谢 Jack 的介绍。

18
00:02:02,240 --> 00:02:09,240
So I was given by Arthur sort of an impossible task.
我被 Arthur 给了几乎不可能完成的任务。

19
00:02:09,240 --> 00:02:17,240
I was requested to explain motivic homotopy theory so that it will be understood by non-mathematicians.
要求我解释母题同伦论，使其能够被非数学家理解。

20
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:21,280
So whatever came out of it, you'll see now,
所以你们现在将会看到结果。

21
00:02:21,280 --> 00:02:31,280
but I don't guarantee that it will be now understandable by either mathematicians or non-mathematicians.
但我不保证这现在对数学家或非数学家来说都能理解。

22
00:02:31,280 --> 00:02:42,280
So what there was at first, so at first there were spaces.
所以最初的情况是，一开始有空间。

23
00:02:42,320 --> 00:02:49,320
So mathematicians were studying spaces and starting with simple examples of spaces.
所以数学家研究空间，并从简单的空间例子开始。

24
00:02:49,320 --> 00:02:52,320
So one of the most basic spaces is a point.
最基本的空间之一是一个点。

25
00:02:52,320 --> 00:02:56,320
There is one which is even more basic, but it's hard to draw.
还有一个更基本的，但很难画出来。

26
00:02:56,320 --> 00:03:03,320
Another one is standard space, which I will have to talk about, is a unit interval.
另一个标准空间，我将不得不讨论的是单位区间。

27
00:03:03,320 --> 00:03:07,320
So an interval of the real line, a line between 0 and 1.
所以实数线上的一个区间，在0和1之间的一条线段。

28
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:15,360
The third example here on the picture is some example of a space of dimension 2.
图片中的第三个例子是一个二维空间的例子。

29
00:03:15,360 --> 00:03:26,360
It's supposed to look like some baking good with two holes in it.
它应该看起来像一个有两孔的烘焙食品。

30
00:03:26,360 --> 00:03:32,360
So the last example is more sophisticated, and I want to include it here.
最后一个例子更复杂，我想把它包括进来。

31
00:03:32,360 --> 00:03:35,360
It's a more sort of mathematical example of a space.
这是一个更数学意义上的空间例子。

32
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:42,400
It's a space of all n by n matrices with complex entries and with non-zero determinant.
这是一个所有 n 乘 n 的复矩阵构成的空间，并且行列式非零。

33
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:46,400
That would be a sophisticated space of dimension n, well,
那将是一个复杂的 n 维空间，好，

34
00:03:46,400 --> 00:03:52,400
depending on how you count, n square or 2n square.
取决于你如何计数，是 n 平方或 2n 平方。

35
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:58,400
So there are many different axiomatizations of the notion of a space in mathematics.
在数学中，有许多不同的空间公理化概念。

36
00:03:58,400 --> 00:04:02,400
For instance, there are topological spaces, there are metric spaces.
比如说，有拓扑空间，有度量空间。

37
00:04:02,440 --> 00:04:04,440
At the end, it all doesn't matter.
最终，这并不重要。

38
00:04:04,440 --> 00:04:11,440
As long as one only considers non-pathological examples,
只要只考虑非病态的例子，

39
00:04:11,440 --> 00:04:13,440
it all comes to the same thing.
它们最终都是一样的。

40
00:04:13,440 --> 00:04:20,440
So I will assume that there is some intuitive understanding of what space is.
因此我将假设对空间的概念有一些直观的理解。

41
00:04:22,440 --> 00:04:25,440
That such understanding is present.
这样的理解是存在的。

42
00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:33,480
So any space, if you formalize it, really write down a definition,
所以任何空间，如果你形式化它，真正写下定义，

43
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:35,480
it will be a tremendously infinite object.
它将是一个极其无穷的对象。

44
00:04:35,480 --> 00:04:37,480
So it's very difficult to work with.
因此很难处理。

45
00:04:37,480 --> 00:04:44,480
So to distinguish spaces mathematically, we use what we call invariance.
为了在数学上区分空间，我们使用所谓的不变量。

46
00:04:44,480 --> 00:04:49,480
So something more understandable, more finite, typically,
因此一些更易于理解、更有限的东西，

47
00:04:49,480 --> 00:04:52,480
than the space itself associated to a space.
比该空间本身通常要多。

48
00:04:52,520 --> 00:04:58,520
So there are two invariants which I will dare to call the most fundamental ones.
所以有两个不变量我敢称之为最基础的。

49
00:04:58,520 --> 00:05:01,520
One is the dimension of a space.
其中一个是空间的维数。

50
00:05:03,520 --> 00:05:08,520
So we have dimension zero for a point and dimension one for the interval.
我们有维度为零的点和维度为一的区间。

51
00:05:08,520 --> 00:05:18,520
And another invariant is the number of pieces the space consists of.
另一个不变量是空间由多少部分组成。

52
00:05:18,560 --> 00:05:24,560
So in this picture, again, the point consists of one piece.
所以在这个图中，点仍然由一个部分组成。

53
00:05:24,560 --> 00:05:27,560
You cannot divide it into two disconnected pieces.
你不能将其分成两个不连通的部分。

54
00:05:27,560 --> 00:05:33,560
And then there is something below the point which is sort of a deformed circle
点下方有一些变形的圆圈，

55
00:05:33,560 --> 00:05:36,560
with some deformed interval sitting inside,
其中有某个变形的区间嵌在里面，

56
00:05:36,560 --> 00:05:39,560
but it consists of two different pieces, two disjoint pieces.
但它由两部分不同且不交的部分组成。

57
00:05:39,560 --> 00:05:41,560
There's a circle and there's an interval.
有一条圆和一条区间。

58
00:05:41,560 --> 00:05:44,560
So the number of pieces is another invariant of a space.
所以部分的数量是空间的另一个不变量。

59
00:05:44,560 --> 00:05:46,560
Typically, when one thinks of a space,
通常，当人们想到一个空间时，

60
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:49,600
one thinks of a space which has only one piece.
他们想到的是只有一个部分的空间。

61
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:56,600
But that's just a custom.
但这只是一种习惯。

62
00:05:56,600 --> 00:06:02,600
So what is homotopy theory about?
所以同伦理论主要研究什么呢？

63
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:10,600
What it does, it basically studies...
它所做的，基本上是研究...

64
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:13,600
Oh, I need to say something.
哦，我需要说一些事情。

65
00:06:13,640 --> 00:06:20,640
Let's call pi zero over space the set of its pieces.
我们可以称空间上的 π₀ 为该空间的组成部分集合。

66
00:06:20,640 --> 00:06:24,640
So if space has two pieces, then pi zero is a set of two elements,
因此，如果空间有两个部分，那么 π₀ 就是一个包含两个元素的集合，

67
00:06:24,640 --> 00:06:26,640
namely these pieces.
即这些部分本身。

68
00:06:26,640 --> 00:06:29,640
So it's typically much more finite than the space itself.
它通常比空间本身要有限得多。

69
00:06:29,640 --> 00:06:34,640
What homotopy theory does, it studies some fancy versions of this invariant,
同伦理论研究这个不变量的一些复杂版本，

70
00:06:34,640 --> 00:06:36,640
which are called higher homotopy sets.
这些被称为高次同伦集。

71
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:42,680
Now, I will try to explain how one gets to these pi n's,
现在，我将尝试解释如何得到这些 πₙ，

72
00:06:42,680 --> 00:06:47,680
where pi n will be some set for any integer n,
其中 πₙ 将是某个集合，对于任何整数 n，

73
00:06:47,680 --> 00:06:50,680
for any, excuse me, non-negative integer n,
对于任何，抱歉，非负整数 n，

74
00:06:50,680 --> 00:06:53,680
how one gets to pi n from pi zero.
从 π₀ 如何得到 πₙ。

75
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:56,680
The first thing which I need to...
首先我需要...

76
00:06:56,680 --> 00:06:58,680
It can be done in different ways.
可以用不同的方法来做。

77
00:06:58,680 --> 00:07:03,680
So I choose to base my explanation on the notion of a continuous map,
所以我选择基于连续映射的概念来解释，

78
00:07:03,720 --> 00:07:07,720
which will also play a fundamental role further.
这个概念将在以后发挥重要作用。

79
00:07:07,720 --> 00:07:09,720
So what is a continuous map?
那么什么是连续映射？

80
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:11,720
So I have a space.
我有一个空间。

81
00:07:11,720 --> 00:07:13,720
This I cannot show on the projection.
这在投影上无法显示。

82
00:07:13,720 --> 00:07:17,720
I have a space n, m, and a space n.
我有一个 n,m 空间，和一个 n 空间。

83
00:07:17,720 --> 00:07:20,720
And a map from one to another is any rule
从第一个空间到另一个空间的映射是任意规则

84
00:07:20,720 --> 00:07:22,720
which assigns to point of the first space
它将第一个空间中的点

85
00:07:22,720 --> 00:07:24,720
and point of the second space.
和第二个空间中的点指定。

86
00:07:24,720 --> 00:07:26,720
The easiest way, of course, to understand it
当然，最容易理解的方式

87
00:07:26,720 --> 00:07:29,720
is by looking at examples.
是通过看例子。

88
00:07:29,760 --> 00:07:31,760
And the idea that it's continuous means
而它连续的意思是

89
00:07:31,760 --> 00:07:33,760
that if something was close,
如果某物靠近，

90
00:07:33,760 --> 00:07:36,760
then it doesn't get too far apart.
那么它不会相差太远。

91
00:07:40,760 --> 00:07:44,760
So let's denote by c of m, n
所以我们用 c(m, n) 表示从 m 到 n 的所有连续映射的集合。

92
00:07:44,760 --> 00:07:48,760
the set of all continuous maps from m to n.
并且我们再次通过例子来说明它是什么。

93
00:07:48,760 --> 00:07:50,760
And we'll see again, by example, what it is.
如果我考虑从一个点到任何空间的连续映射，

94
00:07:50,760 --> 00:07:52,760
If I'm looking at continuous maps
那么从一个点到一个空间的映射是什么呢？

95
00:07:52,760 --> 00:07:55,760
from a point to any space,
它仅仅由这个唯一点映到哪里决定。

96
00:07:55,760 --> 00:07:58,760
so what is a map from a point to a space?
所以从一个点到一个空间的映射

97
00:07:58,800 --> 00:08:02,800
It's just determined by where this unique point goes.
就相当于这个空间中的一个点。

98
00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:04,800
So a map from a point to a space
因此，从一个点到任何空间的映射集合

99
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:06,800
is the same as a point on this space.
与这个空间中的点集是一致的。

100
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:09,800
So the set of maps from the point to any space
(已与上一条字幕合并)

101
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:13,800
is just a set of points of this very same space.
这只是一个空间中点的集合。

102
00:08:13,800 --> 00:08:16,800
Another example is what is the set of maps
另一个例子是任何空间到一个点的映射集是什么？

103
00:08:16,800 --> 00:08:18,800
from any space to a point?
从任意空间到一个点？

104
00:08:18,800 --> 00:08:21,800
There's only one place for all the points
第一空间的所有点只能去一个地方，

105
00:08:21,800 --> 00:08:23,800
of the first space to go,
即目标空间上的唯一一点。

106
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:27,800
namely this only point on the target space.
而从任意空间到这个点的映射只有一个。

107
00:08:27,840 --> 00:08:30,840
And there's always only one map
所以这就是第二个例子。

108
00:08:30,840 --> 00:08:32,840
from any space to the point.
这是一个更复杂的例子。

109
00:08:32,840 --> 00:08:35,840
So that's example number two.
(已与上一条字幕合并)

110
00:08:36,840 --> 00:08:39,840
Here is a more fancy example.
(已与上一条字幕合并)

111
00:08:39,840 --> 00:08:42,840
Let's look at maps
让我们看看从单位区间

112
00:08:44,840 --> 00:08:46,840
from the unit interval,
到任意空间的映射，

113
00:08:46,840 --> 00:08:48,840
the interval of the real line,
实数线上的区间，

114
00:08:48,840 --> 00:08:50,840
to any space.
到任何空间的映射。

115
00:08:50,840 --> 00:08:54,840
So it will have some beginning
所以它会有一个起点

116
00:08:54,840 --> 00:08:56,840
where the point zero goes
其中点零被映射到

117
00:08:56,880 --> 00:08:57,880
or point one goes,
或者点一被映射到，

118
00:08:57,880 --> 00:08:59,880
and then there will be all the points
然后所有介于零和一之间的数字会被映射到所有的中间点。

119
00:08:59,880 --> 00:09:02,880
where all the numbers between zero and one go.
因此，它是连续映射。

120
00:09:02,880 --> 00:09:04,880
So the fact that it's a continuous map
(已与上一条字幕合并)

121
00:09:04,880 --> 00:09:08,880
means that this gadget will have no breaks in it.
这意味着这个装置不会有断点。

122
00:09:08,880 --> 00:09:10,880
That's what it intuitively means.
这就是它的直观含义。

123
00:09:10,880 --> 00:09:12,880
So the set of all continuous maps
所以从区间到任意空间的所有连续映射

124
00:09:12,880 --> 00:09:15,880
from the interval to any space
就是一个空间内的路径集合。

125
00:09:15,880 --> 00:09:19,880
is just a set of paths inside this space.
现在让我们回到空间连通分支的概念。

126
00:09:27,840 --> 00:09:29,840
Now let's go back to the notion
我们如何正式地说两个点属于同一个连通分支？

127
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:32,840
of the number of pieces of a space.
当两点位于同一个连通分支时，

128
00:09:34,840 --> 00:09:37,840
How can we say formally
(已与上一条字幕合并)

129
00:09:37,840 --> 00:09:40,840
when two points lie in the same piece?
(已与上一条字幕合并)

130
00:09:40,840 --> 00:09:42,840
So if they lie in the same piece,
(已与上一条字幕合并)

131
00:09:42,840 --> 00:09:44,840
then they can be connected by a path.
然后它们可以通过一条路径连接。

132
00:09:44,840 --> 00:09:46,840
In different pieces,
在不同的部分，

133
00:09:46,840 --> 00:09:48,840
there's no way you can find a path
你无法找到一条不中断的路径

134
00:09:48,840 --> 00:09:51,840
without breaks which connects one point to another.
将一个点连接到另一个点。

135
00:09:51,840 --> 00:09:54,840
So to define formally
因此为了正式定义

136
00:09:54,840 --> 00:09:57,840
what it means for two points to belong to the same piece,
两点属于同一部分的意义，

137
00:09:57,840 --> 00:09:59,840
one can use this notion of a path,
可以使用路径的概念，

138
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:02,840
of a continuous map from interval to the space.
即从区间映射到空间的连续映射。

139
00:10:06,840 --> 00:10:09,840
So let me repeat myself again.
所以我再重复一遍。

140
00:10:09,840 --> 00:10:12,840
So the only thing which one needs to know
因此唯一需要知道的是

141
00:10:14,840 --> 00:10:17,840
to define the set pi zero of n,
要定义 π₀(n) 的集合，

142
00:10:17,840 --> 00:10:19,840
the set of pieces,
该集合中的元素是各个部分，

143
00:10:19,840 --> 00:10:22,840
is to know what are points and what are paths
就是要知道哪些是点，哪些是从这些点出发的路径。

144
00:10:22,840 --> 00:10:25,840
between these points.
这些点之间的路径。

145
00:10:30,840 --> 00:10:33,840
Well, this is a little bit more fancy,
嗯，这稍微有点复杂，

146
00:10:33,840 --> 00:10:37,840
and maybe I'm not able to explain it as good.
我可能无法解释得特别好。

147
00:10:37,840 --> 00:10:40,840
Now here I'm moving to the next invariant,
现在我转移到下一个不变量，

148
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:42,840
next homotopy set pi one.
下一个同伦群 π₁。

149
00:10:42,840 --> 00:10:44,840
As I said, pi zero is the starting point
如我所说，π₀ 是一系列同伦群的起点。

150
00:10:44,840 --> 00:10:48,840
of an infinite series of homotopy sets.
一系列同伦群。

151
00:10:48,840 --> 00:10:51,840
So what one does for pi zero,
所以对于 π₀，

152
00:10:51,840 --> 00:10:53,840
one takes points
一个取点，

153
00:10:53,840 --> 00:10:57,840
and identifies sort of those
然后将那些可以通过路径连接的点视为相同。

154
00:10:57,840 --> 00:11:00,840
which can be connected by a path.
现在我固定两个点 P 和 Q。

155
00:11:00,840 --> 00:11:03,840
Now suppose I fix two points, P and Q.
现在让我们考虑所有连接它们的路径。

156
00:11:03,840 --> 00:11:06,840
Now let's consider all the paths which connect them.
假设它们落在同一个连通分支上，

157
00:11:06,840 --> 00:11:08,840
Suppose they land the same piece,
所以存在一条路径连接它们。

158
00:11:08,840 --> 00:11:10,840
so there is some path which connects them.
让我们来看所有的路径。

159
